family: web-ui
what: poll
transport: v3
address: 192.0.2.10
verification: reference
reference: RFC 3416 (SNMP operations), RFC 3414 (SNMPv3 users)
does: The values to enter in the device's SNMP agent page so Woodshed can poll it (SNMPv3, read-only).
check: Devices → Add polling → Test poll answers with the device's name and interfaces.
placeholders: <V3-USER> <AUTH-PASSPHRASE> <PRIV-PASSPHRASE>
addresses: 192.0.2.10 2001:db8::10 logs-01.example.net logs-01
notes:
- Reference only: not tested on a device; check your device's documentation.
- Add the same user in Woodshed: Settings → SNMP → v3 users, with the same name, protocols and passphrases.
- Then add the device in Woodshed: Devices → Add polling, its address, SNMPv3 and the user <V3-USER>.
- Field names differ between devices; some also need SNMP allowed on the interface Woodshed reaches.
---- part steps "": In the device's web page, open its SNMP agent settings and enter
SNMP agent: on
SNMP version: v3
User name: <V3-USER>
Security level: authentication and privacy (authPriv)
Authentication: SHA-256, passphrase <AUTH-PASSPHRASE>
Privacy: AES-128, passphrase <PRIV-PASSPHRASE>
Access: read-only
Allowed managers (if asked): 192.0.2.10
